  "invariants": [
    "Operational battlefield pressure is a command-position signal, not automatic casualties or victory.",
    "battle_resolve remains exact casualty and local combat outcome authority.",
    "Formations redeploy through sector edges with elapsed time and do not contribute to either endpoint while in transit.",
    "Battlefield reports become player-visible only after physical command-channel latency unless Tang Wei directly commands in that sector.",
    "Sector assignment never changes formation ownership, administrative authority, strategic location, occupation, or sovereignty.",
    "Operational owners retain current battlefield state and bounded recent reports only; durable battle chronology belongs to authoritative event and battle owners rather than an ever-growing battlefield history tail.",
    "A coarse exact formation may project frontage into multiple adjacent sectors only through conserved sector_commitments_milli shares that sum to exactly 1000; sector presence never duplicates manpower.",
    "Exact local battle contact scales represented bodies, ammunition expenditure, contact wear, cohesion shock, mount exposure, and casualties to each formation's conserved commitment in that sector.",
    "One exact formation owner cannot enter two simultaneous exact battle transactions at the same battlefield timestamp even when its operational frontage spans multiple sectors; non-selected sectors continue through pressure until a later exact contact boundary."
  ],
  "autonomous_contacts": {
    "enabled": true,
    "review_interval_minutes": 90,
